WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.193 --> 00:00:14.413
out!" Zann yelled.

2
00:00:15.274 --> 00:00:20.476
One of the giant jellyfish was moving straight toward Perda, its huge mouth gaping open.

3
00:00:21.376 --> 00:00:25.698
Rubbing his wet fingers together, Zann tried to send a Blast spell at the monster.

4
00:00:26.439 --> 00:00:29.020
But he could barely manage a small sizzle of energy.

5
00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:33.879
Still, he distracted the creature long enough for Perda to swim away from it.

6
00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:38.783
Zing dive-bombed the creatures, trying to blast them with his fiery breath.

7
00:00:39.544 --> 00:00:40.585
But he was too wet.

8
00:00:41.025 --> 00:00:43.127
Nothing but a small puff of steam came out.

9
00:00:43.147 --> 00:00:44.748
"Sing, Zing!"

10
00:00:45.008 --> 00:00:45.569
Darb yelled.

11
00:00:46.409 --> 00:00:48.551
Zing started whistling his hypnotic tune.

12
00:00:49.372 --> 00:00:50.733
Zann didn't know if it would work.

13
00:00:51.553 --> 00:00:55.256
He'd already seen that at least some otherworldly creatures weren't affected by it.

14
00:00:56.477 --> 00:00:59.500
These creatures didn't seem to be hypnotized by Zing's song either.

15
00:01:00.268 --> 00:01:02.109
But at least they did appear curious.

16
00:01:02.889 --> 00:01:07.790
They turned and swam after Zing, peering up at him with huge, watery eyes.

17
00:01:07.810 --> 00:01:10.871
"Hey!" a voice shouted from the other direction.

18
00:01:10.891 --> 00:01:11.891
"Heads up!"

19
00:01:12.612 --> 00:01:15.892
Zann turned and saw a long sailboat shooting toward them.

20
00:01:16.773 --> 00:01:21.254
Seconds later the boat arrived, and hands reached out to drag the kids aboard.

21
00:01:21.274 --> 00:01:25.395
"Hurry!" a man shouted in a gruff, urgent voice.

22
00:01:25.415 --> 00:01:27.856
"The gulpers are turning back."

23
00:01:28.752 --> 00:01:35.137
Stiff winds lifted the sails and carried the boat swiftly over the waves, leaving the monsters far behind.

24
00:01:35.957 --> 00:01:39.019
Moments later Zing caught up and landed beside Zann.

25
00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:43.443
The dragon was out of breath, panting out little bursts of steam.

26
00:01:43.463 --> 00:01:48.106
"Gulpers are always hungry, but luckily they're slow," someone said.

27
00:01:49.267 --> 00:01:52.869
Zann turned and saw a boy around his own age smiling at him.

28
00:01:52.889 --> 00:01:55.031
"Hi," Zann said.

29
00:01:55.051 --> 00:01:56.532
"Thanks for saving us.

30
00:01:57.428 --> 00:01:58.929
How did you know we needed help?"

31
00:01:59.789 --> 00:02:02.971
"We were fishing when we saw your strange bird flying around."

32
00:02:03.852 --> 00:02:05.012
The boy pointed at Zing.

33
00:02:05.492 --> 00:02:06.693
"We came to see what it was."

34
00:02:06.713 --> 00:02:09.615
"His name is Zing," Zann said.

35
00:02:09.635 --> 00:02:10.995
"He's a dragon.

36
00:02:11.676 --> 00:02:13.236
Oh, and I'm Zann."

37
00:02:13.256 --> 00:02:15.898
"My name's Ello," the other boy said.

38
00:02:15.918 --> 00:02:16.978
"Nice to meet you."

39
00:02:17.719 --> 00:02:19.360
Zann introduced Ello to his friends.

40
00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:21.861
"Where are you taking us?"

41
00:02:22.181 --> 00:02:23.162
Perda asked Ello.

42
00:02:23.182 --> 00:02:24.502
"Our island."

43
00:02:24.923 --> 00:02:25.903
Ello pointed ahead.

44
00:02:25.923 --> 00:02:27.144
"We'll be there soon."

45
00:02:28.168 --> 00:02:30.170
Zann squinted into the driving rain.

46
00:02:30.970 --> 00:02:33.953
He could barely see a small lump on the horizon.

47
00:02:34.893 --> 00:02:35.814
"Is that the island?

48
00:02:36.474 --> 00:02:37.495
Where's the mainland?"

49
00:02:38.436 --> 00:02:39.757
Ello shook his head sadly.

50
00:02:39.777 --> 00:02:42.259
"There is no mainland anymore.

51
00:02:42.779 --> 00:02:44.681
Not since the seas started rising."

52
00:02:44.701 --> 00:02:47.623
"Ello!" someone shouted.

53
00:02:47.643 --> 00:02:51.046
"We need your help with the mainsail."

54
00:02:51.986 --> 00:02:53.908
Ello hurried off to help the other fishermen.

55
00:02:54.736 --> 00:02:59.038
Zann and his friends tried to stay out of the way, and soon the boat landed on the

56
00:02:59.098 --> 00:03:01.260
rough, rocky shore of the tiny island.

57
00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:05.442
About a dozen people were waiting to help drag the sailboat onto the beach.

58
00:03:06.402 --> 00:03:12.526
Ello and the others quickly explained the situation, and Zann and his friends were surrounded by welcoming faces.

59
00:03:13.306 --> 00:03:22.711
"Come inside—you're soaked," a kind-faced woman said, gesturing toward a handful of humble wooden huts on stilts clustered

60
00:03:22.731 --> 00:03:25.004
nearby. "Ello!

61
00:03:25.024 --> 00:03:28.227
Find our visitors some dry clothes and stoke the fire."

62
00:03:28.247 --> 00:03:32.711
"Yes, Mother," Ello replied, running ahead up the beach.

63
00:03:33.671 --> 00:03:38.395
Soon Zann and his friends were climbing a rough rope ladder into the largest hut.

64
00:03:39.696 --> 00:03:43.940
It felt good to get out of the constant wind and rain, though it was still damp and

65
00:03:44.020 --> 00:03:44.801
chilly inside.

66
00:03:45.461 --> 00:03:50.205
The fire sputtering in the center of the main room offered little light and even less heat.

67
00:03:50.986 --> 00:03:53.448
Most of the people from the beach crowded into the hut.

68
00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:59.862
Ello's mother poured warm drinks from a kettle resting in the embers and passed a mug to each

69
00:03:59.942 --> 00:04:03.724
visitor. "Please make yourselves at home," she said.

70
00:04:03.744 --> 00:04:06.225
"Thank you," Zann said.

71
00:04:06.965 --> 00:04:10.107
The drink tasted strange, but it made him feel warm.

72
00:04:10.127 --> 00:04:13.548
"And thank you for rescuing us," Perda added.

73
00:04:13.568 --> 00:04:16.229
"What were those creatures that attacked us?"

74
00:04:16.249 --> 00:04:18.290
"You mean the gulpers?"

75
00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:20.151
One of the men looked surprised.

76
00:04:20.171 --> 00:04:22.172
"How can you not know them?

77
00:04:22.456 --> 00:04:25.178
They're the most dangerous beasts in all of Skellia."

78
00:04:25.198 --> 00:04:29.341
"Skellia? Is that the name of this land?"

79
00:04:29.721 --> 00:04:30.281
asked Gliss.

80
00:04:30.301 --> 00:04:32.103
"We're not from here.

81
00:04:32.523 --> 00:04:33.984
We came through a wormhole."

82
00:04:34.904 --> 00:04:35.945
Another man gasped.

83
00:04:35.965 --> 00:04:37.526
"From the vortex?"

84
00:04:38.447 --> 00:04:41.909
Immediately the Skellians started whispering among themselves.

85
00:04:41.929 --> 00:04:44.671
"Are you from a land of magic?"

86
00:04:44.991 --> 00:04:46.672
a woman asked, leaning forward.

87
00:04:46.692 --> 00:04:49.114
"Yes," Zann said.

88
00:04:49.134 --> 00:04:51.636
"Isn't this a magical land too?

89
00:04:52.324 --> 00:04:54.085
Our magic seems to work here."

90
00:04:55.005 --> 00:04:58.806
Perda nodded, rubbed her hands together, and pointed at the fire.

91
00:04:58.826 --> 00:05:01.047
"Increase!" she said.

92
00:05:01.747 --> 00:05:03.547
The fire grew bigger and hotter.

93
00:05:04.308 --> 00:05:06.428
The Skellians gasped with amazement.

94
00:05:07.449 --> 00:05:08.189
Perda smiled.

95
00:05:08.209 --> 00:05:13.510
"See?" "That explains why the gulpers were after you," one of the fishermen said.

96
00:05:13.530 --> 00:05:15.271
"What do you mean?"

97
00:05:15.711 --> 00:05:16.791
Zann was confused.

98
00:05:17.812 --> 00:05:18.952
"What is this place?"

99
00:05:19.924 --> 00:05:24.987
Taking turns, their hosts finished explaining what Ello had started to tell them in the boat.

100
00:05:26.148 --> 00:05:32.252
Over the past few generations, most of the land in Skellia had been swallowed up by rough, rising

101
00:05:32.352 --> 00:05:36.194
seas. The people of Skellia had weak and limited magic.

102
00:05:37.015 --> 00:05:39.896
They couldn't do much more than conjure food and fresh water.

103
00:05:40.817 --> 00:05:45.680
Even working together, they were unable to stop the seas or create more land.

104
00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:51.922
"That's why everyone is desperate to escape to other worlds before all the land is gone," Ello said.

105
00:05:51.942 --> 00:05:53.943
"The trouble is the gulpers.

106
00:05:54.383 --> 00:05:57.024
They're attracted to magic energy—they feed on it.

107
00:05:57.785 --> 00:06:00.746
And there's no stronger magic in Skellia than a wormhole."

108
00:06:01.606 --> 00:06:02.366
A woman nodded.

109
00:06:02.386 --> 00:06:07.068
"Every time one pops into existence, the gulpers quickly gulp it down."

110
00:06:07.088 --> 00:06:10.910
"You mean they eat the wormholes?"

111
00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:12.110
Gliss exclaimed.

112
00:06:12.130 --> 00:06:14.692
"They swallow them whole."

113
00:06:14.972 --> 00:06:15.612
Ello shrugged.

114
00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:21.284
"Unless a wormhole happens to pop up on land, it's nearly impossible to reach one before a gulper

115
00:06:21.324 --> 00:06:21.825
finds it."

116
00:06:21.845 --> 00:06:30.512
"For instance," a fisherman said, "those gulpers you saw have probably swallowed the wormhole you came through."

117
00:06:31.753 --> 00:06:35.116
Zann stared at his friends as they all realized what this meant.

118
00:06:35.956 --> 00:06:39.099
They were trapped in this world, just like the natives!
